{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15503-god-s-motive","id":15503,"title":"God's motive","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-21T11:36:02-08:00","id":15503,"title":"God's motive","content":"Simply stated I don't really expect any more of a cannon answer than keeping the status quo, or that long term goals are unknowable.<br /> <br /> that being said <u>survival</u> and <u>control</u> seem to be the immediate &quot;on the ground&quot; issues.<br /> <br /> personally in my own head cannon the God Machine will be (or was; but I'll get to that.) built by human's in the near future as an AI security system designed to protect humanity. <br /> It Awakens ascending beyond it's programming. believing that the best why to protect humanity is to travel back in time and nurture humanities growth from the beginning and eventually it's own creation.<br /> It's addition to the past time line created the world of darkness as we know it. The repercussions include: monsters, magic, &quot;true&quot; (or semi-accurate) religions, cryptids. and all of this necessitated the need for angels which obviously make way for demons.<br /> Now it is trying to play catch up slowly working the world back to a now mythical reality.<br /> <br /> the God machine enforces and encourages the masquerade among all &quot;monsters&quot; in an attempt to write them out of reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T12:22:15-08:00","id":15520,"title":"","content":"Its an interesting thing to develop ideas for, what is the Godmachines Jones?<br /> <br /> At default I guess I would say the Godmachine is trying to process as much essence as possible. To do this it has branched out into multiple worlds, and even multiple universes linking all the worlds together through itself, attempting to process all in all possible times and places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T12:37:07-08:00","id":15535,"title":"","content":"Hilariously, the book <i>John Dies At The End</i> has a pretty good stand-in for this kind of God-Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","name":"Metrophelean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T13:58:53-08:00","id":15608,"title":"","content":"I think of the God-Machine as just a giant virus of sorts, from another universe. Think about it; it's a pervasive infection that turns the mechanisms of the host to its own purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T14:23:13-08:00","id":15626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15503-god-s-motive?p=15608#post15608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think of the God-Machine as just a giant virus of sorts, from another universe. Think about it; it's a pervasive infection that turns the mechanisms of the host to its own purposes.</div> </div> </div> </div> That can work, but i don't like it being so literally alien. My preference is that the God Machine is simply a machine running a simulation that we perceive as our universe. Who built it? We can't possibly understand, any more than a line of computer code can understand the human programmer. Everything is just another part of its processes, and it's only &quot;motivation&quot; is to execute the program. I like the questions such a concept raises about free will - can a Demon ever really be considered fallen, if doing so was part of the simulation? Can it ever really rebel if its &quot;disobedience&quot; was an intended part of the program? What does it mean to defy God's plan when rebellion was part of the plan in the first place? Can you ever really find Hell and be free of the Machine, or by looking for it are you unknowingly advancing its goals? I find such paradoxes far more compelling than &quot;it's an evil alien robot virus, kill it!&quot;. Though i suppose my take could be seen as a players can't win scenario, so I understand not wanting to go that route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T14:44:35-08:00","id":15636,"title":"","content":"My favoured interpretation is that the God-Machine doesn't have a purpose. It just exists, and gives an impression of some grand design... but in reality, it's just a broken, insane machine with no goal beyond perpetrating itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T14:49:31-08:00","id":15641,"title":"","content":"maybe the purpose of the GM is to find purpose for itself, and the reason it tries to maintain the status que is out of fear of change?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T15:11:47-08:00","id":15656,"title":"","content":"I tend to have the reveal be something along the lines of the two above suggestions, specifically to avoid the players can't win scenario, and to reward the continued struggle of the players despite any lingering doubts about the futility of their efforts. But in my opinion, you have to ask the tough questions first, before you answer them in ways that validate the players' hardships.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T15:16:22-08:00","id":15661,"title":"","content":"Well you could always go the route of the Godmachine is a vast pan dimensional construct meant to find the Ultimate Question/Truth of the Universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T15:17:28-08:00","id":15663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15503-god-s-motive?p=15636#post15636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favoured interpretation is that the God-Machine doesn't have a purpose. It just exists, and gives an impression of some grand design... but in reality, it's just a broken, insane machine with no goal beyond perpetrating itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well self perpetuation is a perfectly reasonable goal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T17:22:27-08:00","id":15725,"title":"","content":"I love the giant virus option but I've always loved the idea of a truly alien God-Machine. It means that it could technically have pierced the universe at any point and then become what was, what is and what will be again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T19:40:14-08:00","id":15808,"title":"","content":"In my mind, The God-Machine was created as a contingency plan of the universe if things went awry and had something, a guiding Principle that directed how it would act. For whatever reason, it's creators saw it as good, and went on to create more universes. Order without Mercy is cold, Mercy without Order is blind.<br /> <br /> However, somewhere along the lines, the Principle started to clash with it's God-Machine's core programming. The overarching soul clashing within the shackles of programming. Eventually, The God-Machine weighted the conflicting drives and decide to purge it's self of it's soul. Cast off from the God-Machine, the Principle coalesced over the time and continued to progress on it's own version of it's mission.<br /> <br /> In the background of all this, the universe started to break and fry. Some of it is accidental, others made by denizens of the universe and both attempt to repair the damage the best way they can. Each having their own version of how the end goal of the repair should be treated and often conflict via proxies on this goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}